---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="Internist-in-training, curious clinical developer, and lifelong learner.">
  <section class="wrap about">
    <aside class="side">
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/images/portrait.webp" alt="Portrait of Gus Bhas in a white coat" width="720" height="664" />
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="main-col">
    <header class="page-head head">
      <p class="eyebrow kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I'm Gus Bhas</h1>
      <p>
        I'm an internist-in-training based in Bali (IDN), a curious clinical developer, and a lifelong learner exploring the
        intersection of clinical medicine, health informatics, creativity, and human connection.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>I believe meaningful progress begins with understanding people, building with intention, and sharing what matters.</p>

      <h2>What Shapes My Perspective</h2>
      <p>
        Grounded in a desire to understand myself and others on a personal level, one question keeps guiding me:
        <strong>how can care be personalized, evidence-based, and holistic at the same time?</strong>
      </p>
      <p>Beyond data and diagnoses, there is the person living with the disease.</p>
      <p>
        I keep learning that clinical data tell only part of the story.
        Understanding the person behind them takes context, curiosity, and human connection. Yet personalizing care
        also means understanding how each person's clinical characteristics differ from others in a similar
        population, and that requires clinical informatics and statistics.
      </p>
      <p>I believe the best solutions begin with understanding how medicine, technology, and humanity fit together.</p>
      
      <figure class="inline-photo">
        <img src="/images/yoga-dm-poster.webp" alt="Gus Bhas beside his first scientific poster, on yoga for type 2 diabetes" width="675" height="900" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>My first ever scientific poster.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>What I'm Doing</h2>
      <p>
        As a resident, I was given a three-letter code name for shift scheduling, and I chose “BHS” so it would be
        easy to recognize. Who knew those three letters would come to summarize what I care about: to
        <strong>Build</strong>, <strong>Heal</strong>, and <strong>Share</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        To make room for my growing fascination with technology, I also created <strong>MEDIx</strong> (Medical
        Education Development and Clinical Informatics Exploration). Through MEDIx, I explore the intersection of
        medical science, clinical knowledge, data, and health technology to support more thoughtful healthcare
        solutions.
      </p>
      <p>Different paths, guided by a shared intention: making what we learn and build genuinely useful to people.</p>

      <h2>What I Hope to Contribute</h2>
      <p>
        I'm here to keep learning, turn meaningful questions into practical ideas, and share knowledge that helps
        others think and act more thoughtfully.
      </p>
      <p>
        I believe progress in healthcare is not only about what science and technology make possible, but about how
        they help us care for people.
      </p>
      <p class="motto serif">Understand the human. Build with purpose. Share what matters.</p>
      <p>I'm glad you're here.</p>

      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/work/">Explore my work</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={site.medix} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore MEDIx</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .kicker { color: var(--gold-text); }
  .about { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px; gap: 64px; align-items: start; }
  .main-col { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
  .side { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; position: sticky; top: 32px; padding-top: 72px; }
  .head { padding-bottom: 8px; }
  .photo {
    width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; overflow: hidden; position: relative;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 35%, #c9d6ca, var(--sage));
  }
  .photo img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 8%; transform: scale(1.12) translateY(6%); }
  .photo::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; top: 18px; right: 28px; width: 16px; height: 16px;
    border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--ivory);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .side { grid-column: 1; position: static; padding-top: 40px; }
    .main-col { grid-row: 2; }
    .photo { width: 200px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .head { padding-top: 28px; }
  }
  .inline-photo { margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .inline-photo img { width: 100%; max-height: 420px; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 35%; border-radius: 16px; }
  .inline-photo figcaption { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
  .prose { padding-bottom: 96px; max-width: none; }
  .prose h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 36px; }
  .motto { margin-top: 32px !important; font-size: 22px; font-style: italic; color: var(--forest); }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; }
</style>
